    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[stop reading process.env.NODE in config for nodeBin]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/npm/statusboard/issues/1070</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/npm/statusboard/issues/1070"/>
        <updated>2026-04-17T14:47:31.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36607?u=79d8c114db476a7ecc6328b328f71d9d758368c7&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">Whatever systems are in place when npm is spawned that determine which node bin to use should not be altered when npm itself spawns node.  This potentially leads to differing node runtimes being ran for the same npm operation.</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>wraithgar</name>
            <email>wraithgar@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/wraithgar</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-02-24T21:01:20.000Z</published>
    </entry>
